<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Murom</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Murom is a city in Vladimir Oblast, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>, on the left bank of the Oka. Mentioned in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/primary-chronicle">Primary Chronicle</a> under 862, it was the seat of a principality held by princes of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chernigov">Chernigov</a> line, and it is associated with the saints Peter and Fevronia and the epic hero <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ilya-muromets">Ilya Muromets</a>. Several of its old monasteries and churches stand along the river.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/murom.jpg" alt="Murom" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Alexxx1979 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Murom._Transfiguration_monastery._Transfiguration_Cathedral_and_Saint_Basil_Church_P5231223_2350.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
